  "unity": {
    "doc": "Unity include lists of the DLL roots (W5-1): tools/gen_module_table.py turns entries into src/module_unity_{combat,convenience,fixture}.inl. native_adapter.cpp keeps the code between the slots and pulls a slot with #define UNITY_SLOT_<NAME> / #include \"module_unity.inl\" / #undef. hosts = DLL roots that compile the file (combat = SPLIT_COMBAT, convenience = SPLIT_BASE; the TACTICS_FIXTURE unit-test shell takes every entry); cond = the preprocessor condition the former hand-written include carried. A host that is not the owning module's DLL needs a shared entry.",
    "slots": ["ai_support", "campaign", "departures", "expert", "personnel_policy", "domestic", "links", "modules", "ui_hosts"],
    "units": {"ui": {"doc": "Table-driven UI and map helpers: unified overlay and dialogs, advisor briefing (overlay, HUD), diplomacy intel, CCZ bridge/editor/title/preview, officer rotation, speed buttons, layout wait, save codec, caravan stay, face keep/timing, mediation, drag learn, region officers, damage preview, building destruction, AI trace and the modpack DLL bridge. Merit, recruitment and the personnel nodes stay in the main unit (wired by hand, not by the module table)."}, "terrain": {"doc": "Terrain foam, trees, water diagnostics, renderer (with the season bake/probe it includes) and the terrain editor (부동산 개발: map edits, hex menu, save sidecar)."}},
    "shared": {
      "native_district_intercept.inl": "stateless corps-policy functions compiled into both DLLs by design: the combat module judges at 1EC890 (sortie_dispatch calls blocked() first); without it the convenience module hooks the dispatcher itself (native_district_intercept_link.inl)"
